+# M0 C0.3 — builder response to review round 3
+
+Review: `reviews/M0-C0.3-r3.md` (0 P0, 1 P1, 0 P2), merged from `origin/review/m0-c03-r3` in `176bc18`.
+Implemented per the orchestrator's ruling. All reviewer tests and evidence are kept unchanged, including the new
+`desktop/src/test/c03-r3-page.test.tsx` and `reviews/evidence/M0-C0.3-r3/`.
+
+| Id | Sev | Status | Commits |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C03-R3-01 | P1 | fixed as ruled: completion on the phase span alone; cadence "insufficient samples (n=1)" | `4a53d5b` |
+| Handoff | — | one-sample completion, legacy-log limitation, Windows AVX-512 coverage | `bd7ec3b` |
+
+## C03-R3-01 — valid one-sample completion rejected — **fixed as ruled**
+
+**Analyzer** (`scripts/analyse-canvas-log.py`):
+- **Validation:**
+  - a version-2 run needs **at least one** pan/zoom sample. Zero samples is still rejected as malformed ("pan/zoom
+    frames missing"), even when the run claims a complete span;
+  - completion is judged on the span alone: it must last its declared duration, its samples must lie on it, and the
+    last sample must be the span's end;
+  - version-1 logs keep the two-sample minimum, because without a span the samples are the only proof of completion.
+- **Cadence:**
+  - estimating cadence needs two samples spanning time;
+  - otherwise the run's analysis records `complete: true`, `cadence: "insufficient samples (n=1)"`, `fps: null`,
+    `intervalMs: null` and `meetsTarget: null`;
+  - the report prints that text in the fps column and "not estimated: insufficient samples (n=1) (run complete)" in
+    the target column;
+  - two equal timestamps read "insufficient samples (n=2, zero-length span)". This also removes a division by zero
+    the old estimator would have hit;
+  - no frames are made up, and nothing claims 60 fps or "missed";
+  - runs with two or more samples use the unchanged estimator.
+
+**Page** (`CanvasSpike.tsx`): `summarizeRun` already returned `fps = null` and `meetsTarget = null` for one sample. The
+readout and the status line now say "insufficient samples (n=1)" / "complete; cadence not estimated" instead of a
+dash. The logged data is unchanged.
+
+**Tests:**
+- reviewer: `C03-R3-01: completed 0.1 Hz phase …` and the 0.2 Hz control pass;
+- the R2 page tests (manual, 60 Hz, 1 Hz "missed") still pass, as do R1 tooling 12/12 and R2 tooling 9/9;
+- mine (`analyzer.test.ts`):
+  - **one frame** under a complete span is accepted: complete, cadence "insufficient samples (n=1)", fps, intervals
+    and target all null, the report says "not estimated", nothing says "met", and the page's `summarizeRun` agrees;
+  - **zero frames** under a complete span is rejected with "pan/zoom frames missing";
+  - also rejected: one frame in a version-1 log, one frame with a span shorter than declared, and one frame that is
+    not on the span's end.
+
+## Correction to my round-2 response
+
+I wrote that "every committed canvas log … still validates". That needs one exception, which the reviewer found:
+`reviews/evidence/M0-C0.3-r2/page-slow.json`. It is the reviewer's version-1 counterexample: a complete 1 Hz page
+run saved before phase spans existed. The version-1 rule still rejects it ("frame timestamps shorter than 10000 ms"),
+because a version-1 log cannot prove completion below 10 Hz.
+
+Re-checked at this head: 24 of the 25 tracked raw canvas logs pass, and that file is the only rejection. The 25
+include the reviewer's round-3 one-frame, two-frame and CI logs. The handoff now states the version-1 limitation explicitly.
+
+## Handoff
+
+- The analyzer row describes one-sample completion and the version-1 limitation.
+- SIMD provenance gains CI 39129350790 (Windows **AVX-512**, macOS NEON, Linux AVX2, two processes each, full
+  39-scene/f32 corpus; the reviewer's audit). The "AVX-512 on the current corpus Linux-only" limitation is retired,
+  as the reviewer noted. No SSE4.2-only hardware has been tested, and the SIMD-policy ticket is unchanged.
+
+## Gates
+
+Local (Windows 11, foreground), at the head of this round:
+
+| Gate | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `cargo fmt --all --check` | pass |
+| `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` | pass |
+| `cargo test --workspace --locked` | **87 passed, 1 ignored** (the ruled C0.4 SIMD ticket); no Rust changed this round |
+| `cargo deny --locked check` | pass |
+| `pnpm lint`, `typecheck`, `format:check`, `licenses:check` | pass |
+| `pnpm test` | **30 Vitest files, 266 passed + 3 standing expected failures** (the reviewer's 0.1 Hz test included); 9/9 Node licence tests |
+| `pnpm --dir desktop build` (+ IPC dist check) | pass |
+
+Fixed while running the gate: my first draft of the new test read `intervalMs.p95` on a field that is now nullable,
+which failed `typecheck`. It now uses optional access.
+
+Not re-run this round: the Tauri build, headless self-test and raster `--check`. No Rust, host or rasteriser code
+changed since round 2's gate, where they passed. CI runs them.
+
+The two Windows Security `PickerHost` prompts were left untouched. CI: the run for the pushed head is in the
+orchestrator summary.
